# ============================================================
# Homelab Manager — Environment Variables
# Copy this file to .env and fill in the values.
# Never commit .env to source control.
# ============================================================

# --- General ---
NODE_ENV=production

# --- Frontend ---
# URL the browser uses to reach the backend API
API_URL=http://localhost:10000
FRONTEND_PORT=10001

# --- Backend ---
BACKEND_PORT=10000
REQUEST_BODY_LIMIT=32kb

# --- Managed app stacks ---
# Absolute path to the `apps/` directory of this repository on the host.
# It is bind-mounted into the backend at the same absolute path so that the
# backend can run `docker compose` against each app's compose file.
# Example: /home/youruser/homelab-management/apps
APPS_DIR=/absolute/path/to/homelab-management/apps

# GID of the host's `docker` group, so the backend's non-root user may use the
# mounted Docker socket. Find it with: getent group docker | cut -d: -f3
DOCKER_GID=999

# Allowed CORS origin for the API (usually the frontend URL)
CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:80

# Secret used to sign access JWTs — generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
JWT_SECRET=change_this_to_a_random_secret

# Secret used to sign refresh JWTs (falls back to JWT_SECRET if not set)
# generate with: openssl rand -hex 32
JWT_REFRESH_SECRET=change_this_to_another_random_secret

# Access token lifetime (default: 1h)
JWT_ACCESS_EXPIRES=1h

# Refresh token lifetime (default: 7d)
JWT_REFRESH_EXPIRES=7d

# ============================================================
# --- Cloudflare / public exposure ---
#
# `sudo ./start.sh` PROMPTS for the three values below on first run and writes
# them here for you, so you normally don't fill these in by hand. Set them
# ahead of time only for an unattended install — with no TTY and no values,
# start.sh skips the Cloudflare/NetBird setup rather than hanging.
#
# Everything else in this section is DERIVED and written back by start.sh —
# leave the *_ID values blank.
# ============================================================

# The public domain every exposed service hangs off, e.g. example.com ->
# authelia.example.com, netbird-vpn.example.com, ...
# This is also the single source the Authelia and NetBird configs template
# their hostnames from, so nothing under apps/ hardcodes a domain.
BASE_DOMAIN=

# Cloudflare API token. Create at:
#   https://dash.cloudflare.com/profile/api-tokens -> Create Token
#     -> "Create Custom Token"
#
# Required permissions:
#   Account -> Cloudflare Tunnel -> Edit    (create the tunnel, publish each
#                                            service's ingress route)
#   Zone    -> DNS             -> Edit      (create each hostname's CNAME)
#   Zone    -> Zone            -> Read      (look up the zone + account id
#                                            from BASE_DOMAIN)
#
# Optional, only if you enable CrowdSec's Cloudflare bouncer (see plan.md
# §23.17) — without these the bouncer fails with "Authentication error
# (10000)" while everything else keeps working:
#   Account -> Account Filter Lists -> Edit
#   Zone    -> Firewall Services    -> Edit
#
# Under "Account Resources" / "Zone Resources", scope it to the account and
# the zone for BASE_DOMAIN — it does not need all-account access.
#
# The dashboard reuses this same token for its Exposure settings; start.sh
# seeds it into the database so it's already filled in on first login.
CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN=

# Name for THIS host's Cloudflare Tunnel. Defaults to the machine's hostname.
# Each server needs its OWN tunnel — reusing one tunnel's connector on a second
# machine makes it a replica and Cloudflare load-balances between them, which
# silently breaks routing. start.sh looks the name up and only creates it if
# it doesn't already exist.
TUNNEL_NAME=

# Derived by start.sh from BASE_DOMAIN + the API token — leave blank.
CLOUDFLARE_ACCOUNT_ID=
CLOUDFLARE_ZONE_ID=
CLOUDFLARE_TUNNEL_ID=

# ============================================================
# --- What start.sh CANNOT do for you ---
#
# start.sh installs Docker, creates the tunnel + connector, generates every
# secret it can, templates the per-app configs from BASE_DOMAIN, and seeds the
# dashboard's exposure settings. The list below is everything it can't, in the
# order you'll hit it. Nothing here needs editing in THIS file — it's here
# because this is the file you're already reading on a new install.
#
# BEFORE running start.sh
#   1. Add the domain to Cloudflare and point your registrar's nameservers at
#      it. start.sh looks the zone up; it will not create it. Without this the
#      zone lookup fails and the whole Cloudflare step is skipped with a
#      warning.
#   2. Create the API token (see CLOUDFLARE_API_TOKEN above). A token can't
#      mint itself.
#
# AFTER running start.sh
#   3. Set a real Authelia password. The shipped
#      apps/authelia/config/users_database.yml.example has a PLACEHOLDER hash
#      that cannot authenticate. Generate one with:
#        docker run --rm authelia/authelia:latest \
#          authelia crypto hash generate argon2 --password 'your-password'
#      That file is gitignored on purpose — it holds the hash guarding every
#      app behind SSO, so never commit it.
#   4. Create the dashboard's first admin account at /setup.
#   5. Change Nginx Proxy Manager's default login. It ships as
#      admin@example.com / changeme and NPM forces a change on first login, so
#      the credentials can't be seeded from here. Then enter the NPM URL and
#      those new credentials in the dashboard's Exposure settings — the
#      Cloudflare half is already filled in, the NPM half can't be.
#   6. Enable "Publicly expose this service" per service in the dashboard.
#      That's what actually creates each NPM proxy host, tunnel route and DNS
#      record. start.sh sets up the tunnel, not the routes on it.
#   7. Set any remaining per-app secrets from the dashboard (most are
#      generated automatically; a few apps need real values).
#
# NetBird specifically: once its exposure is enabled it works with no further
# config — point a client at https://netbird-vpn-api.<BASE_DOMAIN> and sign in
# through Authelia. See plan.md §48 for everything that had to be fixed to make
# that true, and §48.5 for what's still open (relay for mobile-data CGNAT, and
# the CLI's device-auth flow).
# ============================================================

# --- Database ---
POSTGRES_DB=homelab
POSTGRES_USER=homelab
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=change_this_password

# Full connection string built from the variables above
# DATABASE_URL is constructed automatically from the variables above.
# Format: postgresql://<POSTGRES_USER>:<POSTGRES_PASSWORD>@database:5432/<POSTGRES_DB>
